description:
FOUND s543w (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-28, base 749eaf0e) while probing #650's `no Mod <a b>`; the same with qw, so not #650's.

    # plib/Pm.pm: package Pm; sub import { shift; print "import: [@_]\n" } sub unimport { shift; print "unimport: [@_]\n" } 1;
    use lib 'plib';
    BEGIN { print "begin\n" }
    no Pm qw(a b);
    print "x\n";

    perl: begin / unimport: [a|b] / x
    PCL : begin / x                  (exit 0, nothing on stderr)

`./pl2cl` emits no form for the `no Pm qw(a b)` statement at all (the `use lib` before it is there).  perl's `no Module
LIST` is `BEGIN { require Module; Module->unimport(LIST) }`; PCL has `p-unimport` (DECIDED: `no lib LIST` = `(p-unimport
"lib" LIST)`, #2464; `no builtin`, `no autodie` #2873) but the general `no` of a module that is not a pragma reaches no
lowering.  Where: Pl/Parser.pm's include processing (the `use` arm emits `p-use`; find what a `no` of a non-pragma does).
NOT TAKEN by s543w (rare; a different cause from #650).
